AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::removeCollateral()
├── when market is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused for PAUSE_TYPE
├── when market is frozen but not paused
│   └── it should remain available
├── given invalid Credit inputs
│   ├── when receiver is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress before other Credit checks
│   ├── when callback data is nonempty
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketCallbacksUnsupported before account and authorization checks
│   ├── when onBehalf is not creditAccount
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketUnauthorizedAccount
│   ├── when onBehalf is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketUnauthorizedAccount
│   ├── when assets is zero and creditAccount has no debt
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when caller is neither creditAccount nor its authorized delegate
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketUnauthorized
│   └── when assets exceeds recorded collateral
│       └── it should revert with arithmetic underflow without changing accounting or custody
├── given Convex strategy is active
│   ├── when reward pool withdrawal reverts
│   │   └── it should propagate the failure and roll back accounting
│   ├── when reward pool withdrawal returns false
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoConvexCreditLineExternalCallFailed
│   └── given a successful withdrawal
│       ├── it should call withdrawAndUnwrap with assets and claim false
│       ├── it should decrease staked collateral by exactly assets
│       ├── it should preserve raw LP that was idle before withdrawal
│       └── it should not claim or forward rewards
├── given Convex strategy is inactive after emergency exit
│   ├── when recovered idle LP covers assets
│   │   ├── it should transfer exactly the removed collateral to receiver
│   │   ├── it should decrease recorded collateral without calling Booster or reward pool
│   │   └── it should preserve unrelated surplus LP held by the market
│   └── when recovered idle LP is insufficient
│       └── it should revert with ERC20InsufficientBalance and preserve collateral accounting
├── given collateral transfer to receiver fails
│   └── it should revert atomically and restore position and Convex state
├── given a withdrawal while debt remains
│   ├── when the remaining position is solvent at maxLtv
│   │   ├── it should succeed and preserve debt assets and shares
│   │   └── it should decrease collateral accounting and Convex stake by assets
│   ├── when the remaining position would be insolvent at maxLtv
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInsufficientUserCollateral and roll back accounting and custody
│   └── when the oracle returns zero or reverts
│       └── it should revert atomically after the attempted unwind
└── given a valid debt-free withdrawal
    ├── when caller is creditAccount
    │   └── it should succeed
    ├── when caller is an authorized delegate of creditAccount
    │   └── it should succeed
    ├── when oracle returns zero or reverts
    │   └── it should still succeed because a debt-free position is solvent without an oracle call
    ├── when IRM accrual reverts
    │   └── it should revert before changing accounting or withdrawing collateral
    ├── when creditAccount borrow shares are zero but residual global debt assets remain
    │   └── it should still permit collateral withdrawal without querying the oracle
    ├── it should accrue interest before changing collateral accounting
    ├── it should decrease creditAccount collateralAssets by assets
    ├── when assets equals all recorded collateral
    │   └── it should set collateralAssets to zero and return all corresponding LP
    ├── it should transfer assets of raw LP to receiver
    ├── it should not change totalSupply totalBorrowed or claimable fees
    ├── it should emit AccrueInterest and RemoveCollateral in order
    ├── it should include caller creditAccount receiver and assets in RemoveCollateral
    └── it should return assets
